4124938/https://looksmax.org/threads/if-you-have-a-long-ramus-its-over-for-you.1274830/"},{"title":"do i have a short ramus and whats the ideal ramus length","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/do-i-have-a-short-ramus-and-whats-the-ideal-ramus-length.1273190/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250114132850/https://looksmax.org/threads/do-i-have-a-short-ramus-and-whats-the-ideal-ramus-length.1273190/"},{"title":"uneven ramus lengths","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/uneven-ramus-lengths.1230120/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20241210102943/https://looksmax.org/threads/uneven-ramus-lengths.1230120/"},{"title":"would testosterone lengthen ramus","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/would-testosterone-lengthen-ramus.1083098/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240804202242/https://looksmax.org/threads/would-testosterone-lengthen-ramus.1083098/"},{"title":"long ramus short mandible","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/long-ramus-short-mandible.1018959/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240511072011/https://looksmax.org/threads/long-ramus-short-mandible.1018959/"},{"title":"question realsurgerymax regarding jaw ramus asymmetry","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/question-realsurgerymax-regarding-jaw-ramus-asymmetry.1004777/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240424200711/https://looksmax.org/threads/question-realsurgerymax-regarding-jaw-ramus-asymmetry.1004777/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Mandible — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandible"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Jawline & face shape","chain":["Implant added along ramus","Jaw height and angle increase","Longer, squarer jawline"],"effect":"direct","text":"A longer, squarer jawline from added height along the vertical jaw. An implant placed along the ramus raises the jaw angle, and the shape change is visible after healing. Very little cosmetic outcome data has been published."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Mandible","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandible"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The mandibular ramus is the vertical portion of the lower jaw that connects the angle of the jaw to the joint near the ear. Ramus augmentation, or vertical ramus augmentation, refers to adding implant material along the ramus to increase its apparent height and the definition of the jaw angle, for a longer, squarer jawline.","Looksmaxxing communities discuss it mainly as one element of custom or wrap-around jaw implant designs. In the sources reviewed, the published literature on ramus implants addresses different questions: dental implants placed in the ramus area for denture support or orthodontic anchorage, and mechanical testing of implants used in jaw reconstruction.[1][2][3][4] No study was found examining ramus augmentation for cosmetic purposes."],"infobox":[["Type","Facial skeletal augmentation (implant)"],["Target","Vertical ramus and jaw angle"],["Typical device","Custom or standard jaw implant"],["Cosmetic outcome data","None found"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Augmenting the ramus differs from widening the jaw at the angle: the goal is added vertical height along the back of the jaw, which affects the look of the jawline in profile. It is commonly mentioned together with chin and angle augmentation in custom jaw implant designs."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Related ramus implant literature","paras":["A 1971 report in a dental implantology journal described observations following use of a ramus implant, a device used for denture support rather than facial contour.[2] A 1992 French paper reported ten years of experience with a mandibular ramus implant framework,[3] and a 2011 Chinese study examined ramus implant anchorage for distalizing the lower dental arch in orthodontics.[4] These are not cosmetic studies.","A 2016 cadaver and finite-element study evaluated how a commercial alloplastic implant fixed to a mandibular ramus transfers load after resection, which concerns reconstruction after tumor or trauma.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found on cosmetic vertical ramus augmentation. Studies of ramus implants in dentistry and reconstruction exist but address different purposes.[1][2][3][4]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Experimental and numerical predictions of Biomet alloplastic implant in a cadaveric mandibular ramus","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27017105/","source":"Journal of Cranio-Maxillo-Facial Surgery","year":2016,"type":"study"},{"title":"The ramus implant: a report on observations following its use","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/5285110/","source":"Oral Implantology","year":1971,"type":"study"},{"title":"Mandibular ramus implant framework. 10 years' experience","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1502468/","source":"Revue de Stomatologie et de Chirurgie Maxillo-Faciale","year":1992,"type":"study"},{"title":"Clinical study of ramus implant anchorage for mandibular arch distalization","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22109368/","source":"Shanghai Journal of Stomatology","year":2011,"type":"study"}],"studies":[{"title":"Experimental and numerical predictions of Biomet alloplastic implant in a cadaveric mandibular ramus","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27017105/","source":"Journal of Cranio-Maxillo-Facial Surgery","year":2016,"kind":null},{"title":"The ramus implant: a report on observations following its use","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/5285110/","source":"Oral Implantology","year":1971,"kind":null},{"title":"Mandibular ramus implant framework. 10 years' experience","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1502468/","source":"Revue de Stomatologie et de Chirurgie Maxillo-Faciale","year":1992,"kind":null},{"title":"Clinical study of ramus implant anchorage for mandibular arch distalization","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22109368/","source":"Shanghai Journal